source: crates/clients/cli/tests/cli/human.rs
expression: "shot(&server, &co, &dir, &[\"help\", \"stacks\"]).await"
---
STACKS

A stack is a chain of unlanded changes, each built on the one below.

    rill new -m "Add lexer"   # first change
    # … edit …
    rill new -m "Use lexer"   # stacked on the first, holding only the new edits

rill log draws the stack on its own lane, joining trunk where it is
based (@ is your working change, ○ the changes under it).

    rill stack show           # the stack, bottom up
    rill stack submit         # open reviews for every change
    rill stack land --wait    # land them in order, as one group

When trunk moves, rill stack sync rebases the stack on the server, and
rill sync moves your checkout onto trunk, merging local edits.
